+++ b/docs/USAGE.md
+#### Proposing Wayfinder Goals and KPIs in a Draft
+
+A project-manager worker can also propose Wayfinder goals, KPI metrics, datapoints and org-level KPIs. These go through the same draft review as task proposals. The chief of staff never writes; nothing reaches Wayfinder until the draft is approved and applied.
+
+| Tool | What it proposes | Applied as |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ta_propose_goal_create` | A goal (`name` required; `description`, `kind`, `parent_goal_id`, `target_date` optional) | `POST /api/projects/<project>/goals` |
+| `ta_propose_kpi_metric_create` | A metric under a goal (`goal_id`, `label`, `unit`, `target`, `cadence`, `kind`, `aggregation` required; `require_gate`, `weight` optional) | `POST .../goals/<goal>/kpi-metrics` |
+| `ta_propose_kpi_datapoint_add` | A reading on a metric (`metric_id`, `value` required; `source` optional) | `POST .../kpi-metrics/<metric>/datapoints` |
+| `ta_propose_kpi_create` | An org KPI (`label` required; `description`, `weight`, `created_by`, `source_ref`, `project_scoped` optional) | `POST /api/orgs/<org>/kpis` |
+
+Every call takes the `goal_run_id` of the worker's goal. Inputs are validated when the proposal is captured, so a bad one is rejected before a reviewer sees it: numbers must be finite and within +-1e12, `cadence` is one of `none`, `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly`, metric `kind` is `task_count` or `external`, `aggregation` is `sum` or `latest`, and names and descriptions have length caps. The project is always the one configured under `[plan.wayfinder]`; a proposal cannot name another.
+
+Proposals can depend on each other. Each call returns an `index`, its position in the draft. A later proposal may pass `ref:<index>` instead of an id, and at apply time that resolves to the id Wayfinder returned for the earlier step:
+
+```text
+ta_propose_goal_create          -> index 0
+ta_propose_kpi_metric_create    goal_id = "ref:0"   -> index 1
+ta_propose_kpi_datapoint_add    metric_id = "ref:1" -> index 2
+```
+
+A ref must point at an earlier proposal of the right kind. Datapoints cannot be added to a `task_count` metric, because Wayfinder derives those from task state; use an `external` metric.
+
+Review and apply work as for task proposals:
+
+```bash
+ta draft view <draft-id>     # each proposal is listed with its fields and refs
+ta draft apply <draft-id>    # replays approved proposals against Wayfinder, in order
+```
+
+Proposals are replayed in the order they were made. Each create carries an `external_id` of `ta_draft:<draft-id>:<index>`, so Wayfinder treats a repeat as the same resource. Returned ids are recorded in `.ta/wayfinder-task-replay.log`. If a step fails, or the reviewer rejected it, every step that refs it is skipped and the output names the step that blocked it. Fix the cause and re-run `ta draft apply`: finished steps are not sent again, and refs resolve from the recorded ids.
+
+Failures say which route was called and what to do:
+
+- **403:** the service account lacks a right. Goals, metrics and datapoints need `tasks:write`; org KPIs need `kpis:manage`.
+- **409:** reported as a conflict with Wayfinder's own message and the fix, for example when a datapoint targets a `task_count` metric. Change or drop the proposal in a follow-up draft.
+
